  "announcement_title": "0.0.71 - 2026-10-16",
  "announcement_changelog": "### Fixed\n\n- ca65 configurations with unfilled MEMORY areas now emit their used file extents, preserving internal gaps and CPU addresses without appending unused capacity. Filled empty areas and omitted `.res`/`.align` fill bytes also follow native ld65 output. ([#723](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/pull/723))\n- SjASMPlus logical expressions now work consistently in ASSERT, EQU, data and IF, with native comparison precedence, -1/zero truth values and eager operand evaluation. ([#726](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/pull/726))\n- SjASMPlus shifts now use signed 32-bit operands and intermediate results with native count masking, so expressions such as `1<<32` and `(1<<31)>>31` emit the correct bytes. Oversized numeric literals are rejected. ([#727](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/pull/727))\n- Native ecosystem audit uploads now require the complete report, process logs and generated tables, so a partial upload cannot look like a complete capture. ([#729](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/pull/729))",
  "announcement_github_body": "## Release Notes\n\n### Fixed\n\n- ca65 configurations with unfilled MEMORY areas now emit their used file extents, preserving internal gaps and CPU addresses without appending unused capacity. Filled empty areas and omitted `.res`/`.align` fill bytes also follow native ld65 output. ([#723](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/pull/723))\n- SjASMPlus logical expressions now work consistently in ASSERT, EQU, data and IF, with native comparison precedence, -1/zero truth values and eager operand evaluation. ([#726](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/pull/726))\n- SjASMPlus shifts now use signed 32-bit operands and intermediate results with native count masking, so expressions such as `1<<32` and `(1<<31)>>31` emit the correct bytes. Oversized numeric literals are rejected. ([#727](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/pull/727))\n- Native ecosystem audit uploads now require the complete report, process logs and generated tables, so a partial upload cannot look like a complete capture. ([#729](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/pull/729))\n\n## Install asm198x 0.0.71\n\n### Install prebuilt binaries via shell script\n\n```sh\ncurl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -LsSf https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/releases/download/asm198x-v0.0.71/asm198x-installer.sh | sh\n```\n\n### Install prebuilt binaries via powershell script\n\n```sh\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -c \"irm https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/releases/download/asm198x-v0.0.71/asm198x-installer.ps1 | iex\"\n```\n\n### Install prebuilt binaries via Homebrew\n\n```sh\nbrew install asm198x/tap/asm198x\n```\n\n## Download asm198x 0.0.71\n\n|  File  | Platform | Checksum |\n|--------|----------|----------|\n| [asm198x-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.xz](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/releases/download/asm198x-v0.0.71/asm198x-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.xz) | Apple Silicon macOS | [checksum](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/releases/download/asm198x-v0.0.71/asm198x-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.xz.sha256) |\n| [asm198x-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.xz](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/releases/download/asm198x-v0.0.71/asm198x-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.xz) | Intel macOS | [checksum](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/releases/download/asm198x-v0.0.71/asm198x-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.xz.sha256) |\n| [asm198x-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/releases/download/asm198x-v0.0.71/asm198x-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip) | x64 Windows | [checksum](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/releases/download/asm198x-v0.0.71/asm198x-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip.sha256) |\n| [asm198x-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.xz](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/releases/download/asm198x-v0.0.71/asm198x-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.xz) | ARM64 Linux | [checksum](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/releases/download/asm198x-v0.0.71/asm198x-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.xz.sha256) |\n| [asm198x-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.xz](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/releases/download/asm198x-v0.0.71/asm198x-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.xz) | x64 Linux | [checksum](https://github.com/asm198x/asm198x/releases/download/asm198x-v0.0.71/asm198x-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.xz.sha256) |\n\n",
